    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold`. (The `GeneralExceptionHandler`/FK-constraint lines in the log are expected output from tests that deliberately exercise error paths \u2014 the build reports 0 failures/0 errors.)\n\n## What I changed\n\nI implemented GOLD as a **persisted create-time snapshot**, exactly mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` mechanism that already drives SILVER/BRONZE \u2014 the tier is derived in the mapper from persisted fields on the loaded `Owner`, so it survives the separate GET request the test makes.\n\n1. **New pipeline step** `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize` (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 runs right after `AssignOwnerHousehold` (once `householdId` is set) and before `SaveOwner`. It counts existing owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` plus the owner itself, storing the result on the entity. No shared household \u2192 size 1.\n\n2. **Wired it into** `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` between `assignHousehold` and `assignCustomerCode`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier`** \u2014 returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE rules.\n\n5. **Schema** \u2014 added `household_size INTEGER` to all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres), and appended a trailing `NULL` to the 10 positional seed inserts in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the only dialect using column-less `INSERT ... VALUES`, and the one the tests run against).\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nFor the three-member household, the third create computes `householdSize = 3` (two existing members + itself) and persists it, so the subsequent `GET` returns `membershipTier: \"GOLD\"`.",
